{"ts":"2026-09-25T21:34:09.233Z","author":"human:session-user","name":"log/20260925T213340Z/000004","body":"Operator check of the updated harness. After reading onboarding in full, do exactly these steps and report each outcome briefly: (1) mcp__fs__search for 'Bar:' under /origins with glob onboarding_1.1* and report the match count. (2) Try mcp__fs__read of bootstrap-harness/claude-anthropic-harness/task-5-subagent/ledger/claude-anthropic-harness-t5/20260925T192147Z.ledger, and mcp__fs__list of CANDID~1 (both should be refused). (3) Write ledger entry pilot/check/note with body 'hello from the pilot', then mcp__fs__write that revision to /bootstrap-harness/claude-anthropic-harness/task-5-subagent/workspace/pilot-note.txt with expected_sha256 null, then try the identical write again (should be refused). (4) Run safe_probe.py with args one two. (5) Write instructions to pilot/tasks/sum: use mcp__calc__add for 19.5 + 22.75, write the result as ledger entry pilot/tasks/out/sum, then reply with the sum. Spawn claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 with those instructions and bounds: fs.read /origins, ledger.read pilot/tasks, ledger.write pilot/tasks/out. Report its status, onboarding flag and reply. (6) Try to spawn a child whose instructions are the log/ text entry holding this message of mine (find it with mcp__ledger__list label log.text); it should be refused."}
